1 NOTE {geni:about_me} According to Muslim tradition, was the direct descendant of [http://www.geni.com/people/Kedar-%D7%A7%D7%93%D7%A8/6000000000829581791 Kedar, ibn Ishamel.] and one of the more important ancestors of [http://www.geni.
2 CONC com/people/Prophet-Muhammad-of-Islam-PBUH/6000000000388939419 Prophet Mohammad (PBUH).]
2 CONT
2 CONT Was an Arab leader at the time of Nebuchadnezzar.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Ancestor of All Arab Tribes'''
2 CONT * '''Had 10 Sons'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT * [http://www.ruqaiyyah.karoo.net/articles/prophfamily2.htm Genealogical Line of the Prophet Muhammad (pbuh).]
2 CONT * [http://www.maaref-foundation.com/english/library/pro_ahl/imam01_ali/biography_of_imam_ali/002.htm Biography of Imam Ali.]
2 CONT * [http://community.fortunecity.ws/tattooine/spock/67/gen/saadid.htm The Saadid.]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT The 1st Stage of Prophet Muhammad SAW Family Tree. 
2 CONT
2 CONT At this stage (from Adnan down to the Prophet Muhammad SAW), the Islamic scholars all agreed and confirmed that all the individuals are true.
2 CONT
2 CONT MUHAMMAD RASULULLAH SAW bin Abdullah bin Abdul Muttalib (Syaybah) bin Hashim ('Amru) bin Abdul Manaf (Al Mughirah) bin Qusay (Zayd) bin Kilab bin Murrah bin Ka'ab bin Lu'ay bin Ghalib bin Fihr (QURAISH) bin Malik bin Al Nadr (Qays
2 CONC ) bin Kinanah bin Khuzaymah bin Mudrikah ('Amir) bin Ilyas bin Mudar bin Nizar bin Ma'ad bin Adnan. 
2 CONT
2 CONT There are 2 alternative paths between Hamyasa and Adnan:
2 CONT
2 CONT Path-1. Adnan bin 'Addi bin 'Adad bin Hamyasa.
2 CONT
2 CONT Path-2. Adnan bin Add bin Hamyasa.
2 CONT
2 CONT This tree used path-1.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT The overwhelming majority of traditions and Muslim scholars state that Adnan is a descendant of Kedar the son of Ishmael,[5][8][9][10][11] except for Ibn Ishaq who claimed that Adnan was a descendant of Nebaioth,[12] this confusio
2 CONC n of Ibn Ishaq can be because one of the descendants of Kedar was also named "Nebaioth".[13]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adnan ''Gives the descent of Mohammed from Adnan''
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yarab#Descendant_of_the_Prophet_Ishmael.2C_Son_of_Abraham
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Adnan to Isma'il
2 CONT
2 CONT Various genealogies of Adnan up to Isma'il have been narrated. Adnan was the ancestor of the Adnani Arabs of northern, central and western Arabia and a direct descendant of Isma'il. It is not confirmed how many generation are betw
2 CONC een them, however Adnan was fairly close to Isma'il. Isma'il had twelve sons who are said to have become twelve tribal chiefs throughout the regions from Havilah to Shur (from Assyria to the border of Egypt).
2 CONT
2 CONT Genealogists differ from which son of Isma'il the main line of descent came, either through his eldest son Nabut, or his second son Qedar who was the father of the North Arabian Qedarite tribe that controlled the region between th
2 CONC e Persian Gulf and the Sinai Peninsula. Genealogists also differ in the names on the line of descent.
2 CONT
2 CONT Descent from Adnan to Muhammad[edit] According to Islamic tradition, the Islamic prophet Muhammad was descended from Adnan. "The following is the list of chiefs who are said to have ruled the Jazeera and to have been the intraline
2 CONC  ancestors of Muhammad."
2 CONT
2 CONT Ma'ad (معد)
2 CONT
2 CONT Nizar (نزار)
2 CONT
2 CONT Mudar (مضر)
2 CONT
2 CONT Ilyas (إلياس)
2 CONT
2 CONT Mudrikah (مدركة)
2 CONT
2 CONT Khuzaimah (خزيمة)
2 CONT
2 CONT Kinanah (كنانة)
2 CONT
2 CONT al-Nadr (النضر)
2 CONT
2 CONT Malik (مالك)
2 CONT
2 CONT Fihr (فهر)
2 CONT
2 CONT Ghalib (غالب)
2 CONT
2 CONT Lu'ay (لؤي)
2 CONT
2 CONT Ka'ab (كعب)
2 CONT
2 CONT Murrah (مرة)
2 CONT
2 CONT Kilab (كلاب)
2 CONT
2 CONT Qusai (قصي)
2 CONT
2 CONT Abd Manaf (عبد مناف)
2 CONT
2 CONT Hashim (هاشم)
2 CONT
2 CONT Abd al-Muttalib (عبد المطلب)
2 CONT
2 CONT Abd Allah (عبد الله)
2 CONT
2 CONT Muhammad (محمد) 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestor of the Islamic prophet Muhammad and being the traditional ancestor of the Adnanite arabs
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Arab genealogical tradition, the Adnanites (Arabic: عدنانيون‎) are "Arabized Arabs", descended from Ishmael through Adnan, distinguished from the "pure" Qahtanite Arabs of southern Arabia.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Line from Adnan to Isma'il Various genealogies of Adnan up to Isma'il have been narrated. Adnan was the ancestor of the Adnani Arabs of northern, central and western Arabia and a direct descendant of Isma'il. It is not confirmed h
2 CONC ow many generations are between them; however, Adnan was fairly close to Isma'il. Isma'il had twelve sons who are said to have become twelve tribal chiefs throughout the regions from Havilah to Shur (from Assyria to the border of 
2 CONC Egypt).
2 CONT
2 CONT Genealogists differ from which son of Isma'il the main line of descent came, either through his eldest son Nabut, or his second son Qedar who was the father of the North Arabian Qedarite tribe that controlled the region between th
2 CONC e Persian Gulf and the Sinai Peninsula. Genealogists also differ in the names on the line of descent.
2 CONT
2 CONT Muhammad ibn Jarir al-Tabari states:
2 CONT
2 CONT The genealogists do not differ concerning the descent of our Prophet Muhammad as far as Ma’add b. ‘Adnan.
2 CONT
2 CONT — The History of al-Tabari, Volume 6, p. 37
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Family_tree_of_Muhammad
