1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY: In Arabic literature, Adnan is held to be a descendant of Ishamel, son of the Semite Abraham and half-brother of Isaac, who was a progenitor of the Jews.  However, all proposed genealogies have failed to include even ha
2 CONC lf of the necessary generations.  When speaking of his own lineage, Muhammad the Prophet wrote, "Beyond Adnan, none but the Lord knows and the genealogists lie."
2 CONT
2 CONT David Hughes (http://members.aol.com/rdavidh218/davidicdynasty.html) argues that the Arabic Adnan ben Udad is identical to the Judaic Adnan ben Judah of Gamala, and is therefore of the house of David.  That lineage is given here.
1 NOTE Muhammad the Prophet never traced his ancestors farther than Adnân, and
2 CONT    declared that all who went back further were guilty of fabrication and
2 CONT    falsehood. "Beyond Adnân none but the Lord knows and the genealogistslie".[Custer February 1, 2002 Family Tree.FTW]
2 CONT
