1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Source 1: [http://www.ruqaiyyah.karoo.net/articles/prophfamily2.htm Prophet's Family.]
2 CONT * Source 2: [http://www.maaref-foundation.com/english/library/pro_ahl/imam01_ali/biography_of_imam_ali/002.htm Biography of Imam Ali - Family & Pedigree.]
2 CONT * Source 3: [http://community.fortunecity.ws/tattooine/spock/67/gen/saadid.htm Saadid.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Biblical age 137
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT In Islamic tradition Lu'ay was an ancestor of Muhammad.
2 CONT
2 CONT In Ibn Ishaq's Biography of the Prophet Muhammad (as translated by Alfred Guillaume) he reports these stories:
2 CONT
2 CONT "A soothsayer Shafi' b. Kulayb al-Sadafi had come to Yemen King Tubba' and lived with him, and when he wished to bid him farewell Tubba' asked him whether he had anything of importance to communicate, and in the customary rhymes o
2 CONC f saj' (light poems) he told him in reply to the question whether any king would fight with Tubba', "No, but the king of Ghassan had a son whose kingdom would be surpassed by a man of great piety, helped by the Almighty, described
2 CONC  in the Psalms (of the Israelites); his people would be favoured by revelation, he would dispel darkness by light, Ahmad the prophet. How blessed his people when he comes, one of the descendants of Lu'ayy from Banu Qusayy. Tubba' 
2 CONC sent for a copy of the psalms, examined them, and found the description of the prophet."
2 CONT
2 CONT Lu'ay's grandson Qusay who conquered Mecca for Quraish said a poem taking pride in his grandfather Lu'ay:
2 CONT
2 CONT I am the son of the protectors from Lu'ayy in Mecca is my house where I grew. mine is the valley as Ma'add knows, It is Marwa I delight in, I did not have to battle, had not, the sons of Qedar and Nabit settled here, Rizh is my he
2 CONC lper I fear no injustice as long as I live"
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lu%27ayy_ibn_Ghalib
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
