1 NAME Abu Ghabshan al-Muhtarish
1 SEX M
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Abū G̲h̲abs̲h̲ān al-Muḥtaris̲h̲ b. Hulail b. Salūl, sold the key of the temple to Ḳuṣaiy b. Kināna, through whom the custodianship came down to the tribe of Ḳurais̲h̲, for a skin of wine. This tribe was divided int
2 CONC o three principal branches: Ḥubs̲h̲īya, ʿAdī and Ḥirmiz, the last of which was probably very small as no notable persons belonging to this clan are mentioned. Ḥubs̲h̲īya was divided into several families, namely: Ḥulail, Ḳumair, Ḍ
2 CONC āṭir, Kulaib and G̲h̲āḍira. To the first belonged al-Muḥtaris̲h̲ mentioned above and Kurz b. ʿAlḳama who followed the Prophet on his flight from Mekka to al-Medīna as far as the cave where he lost trace of him, when he found a spi
2 CONC der-web over the entrance of the cave. He lived to the time of Muʿāwiya and it was through his knowledge of the topography of the country that the limits of the Holy Territory were fixed, which have been retained to this day. Of t
2 CONC he family of Ḳumair was Ḳabīsa b. Ḏh̲uʾaib, who was bom in’ the life-time of the Prophet and died in Syria in 86 a. h., and Mālik b. al-Hait̲h̲am b. ʿAwf, one of the principal emissaries of the ʿAbbāsids and friend of Abū Muslim, 
2 CONC who left him in charge of the army when he went to see the Caliph al-Manṣūr and was murdered.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliography
2 CONT
2 CONT Ibn Duraid, Is̲h̲tiḳāḳ, ed. Wüstenfeld, p. 276 sqq.
2 CONT
2 CONT al-Nuwairī, Nihāyat al-Arab, ed. Cairo, ii. 318 sqq. and 336
2 CONT
2 CONT al-Ḳalḳas̲h̲andī, Nihāyat al-Arab, ed. Bag̲h̲dād, p. 199, 242, 260, 312, 326
2 CONT
2 CONT al-ʿIḳd al-Farīd, ed. Cairo, 1316, ii. 53
2 CONT
2 CONT al-Samʿānī, Ansāb, ed. Margoliouth, Gibb Memorial Series, vol. xx., fol. 304a
2 CONT
2 CONT Ag̲h̲ānī, ix. 93, xv. 53
2 CONT
2 CONT Usd al-G̲h̲āba, ed. Cairo, 1286 (passim)
2 CONT
2 CONT Ibn Ḥad̲j̲ar, Tahd̲h̲īb, ed. Ḥaidarābād, (passim)
2 CONT
2 CONT Wüstenfeld, Genealogische Tabellen and Register.
