1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From ''Banu Saleem'' Clan of ''Banu al-Hawāzin'' Tribe.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source 1: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atikah_bint_Murrah
2 CONT
2 CONT Source 2: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hawazin
2 CONT
2 CONT Source 3: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abd_Manaf_ibn_Qusai
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atikah_bint_Murrah
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atikah_bint_Murrah
2 CONT
2 CONT '''ʿĀtikah bint Murrah ibn Hilāl ibn Fālij ibn Dhakwān''' (Arabic: عاتكة بنت مرة) (fl. 5th century CE) was a Hawazin heiress, and the mother of Hashim ibn 'Abd Manaf, thus the great-great-grandmother of Islamic prophet Muhammad.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT She was daughter of Murrah ibn Hilal and Safiya bint Awf, cousin of Murrah. Atikah was a woman from Banu Hawazin. She married a leader of Banu Ka'b ibn Lu'ayy, Abd Manaf ibn Qusay. By him, she had many sons. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The sons are: 
2 CONT * al-Muttalib (المطلب)
2 CONT * Amr/Hashim (عمرو/هاشم) 
2 CONT * Abd Shams (عبد الشمس)
2 CONT
2 CONT The daughters are: 
2 CONT * Barrah (برة)
2 CONT *  Halah (هالة)
2 CONT * Tumāḍir (تماضر)
2 CONT *  Qilabah (قلابة)
2 CONT * Hayyah (حياة)
2 CONT * Rayta (ريطة)
2 CONT *  Kathamah (خثامة) 
2 CONT * Sufyanah (سفيانة)
