1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Given name also spelled '''Arwa'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Wikipedia's article for her (link above) reports that she married firstly '''ʻAffān bin Abu al-ʻAs''', and secondly '''Uqbah bin Abu Mu'ayt'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source 1: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Urwa_bint_Kariz
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Arwa bint Kurayz (Arabic: أروى بنت كريز‎) was the mother of Uthman ibn Affan, a companion of the Islamic prophet Muhammad, and the third of the Sunni Rashidun or "Rightly Guided Caliphs".
2 CONT
2 CONT Arwa was the daughter of Kurayz ibn Rabi'ah ibn Habib Abd Shams ibn Abd Manaf, so was from the Banu Abd-Shams tribe, a sub-clan of the Quraysh.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arwa's mother was Umm Hakim bint Abdul Muttalib, so Arwa was a cousin of the Islamic Prophet Muhammad.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arwa married Affan ibn Abi al-'As and bore him Uthman and Amina. After the death of Affan, Arwa married Uqba ibn Abu Mu'ayt, to whom she bore al-Walid, 'Ammara, Khalid, Umm Kulthum, Umm Hakim and Hind.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arwa bint Kurayz converted to Islam and emigrated to Madina after her daughter, Umm Kulthum bint Uqba. She gave allegiance to Muhammad and remained in Madina until she died during the caliphate of her son, Uthman ibn Affan.
