1 NOTE Wikipédia fr : Rukayya (arabe ruqayya : élevée), deuxième des quatre filles de Mahomet et Khadija, morte avant son père. Le calife Uthman fut successivement époux et veuf d'elle et de sa soeur Umm Kulthum.  On trouve la forme Roki
2 CONC a en Afrique noire. <li>Wikipédia anglaise : Ruqayyah is a daughter of the Muslim Prophet Muhammad. There are different beliefs as to her biological parents. Some Sunnis and some Shi'a view her as the daughter of Muhammad himself 
2 CONC and his first wife Khadijah bint Khuwaylid, but some Shia and non-Muslims view her as the daughter of Khadijah's assumed previous husband. See Genealogy of Khadijas' daughters.  Ruqayyah's first marriage was to Utbah ibn Abu Lahab
2 CONC , the son of Prophet Muhammad's paternal uncle Abu Lahab, who turned out to be a fierce enemy of Prophet Muhammad from the beginning of his public mission. (ref) Ruqayyah's second marriage was to Uthman ibn Affan, one of Prophet M
2 CONC uhammad's closest companions. Ruqayyah had a son from her second marriage, Abd-Allah ibn Uthman, who died when he was 2 years old. Ruqayyah died in 2 AH (624 CE). [edit]  Contradictory beliefs  Sunnis believe the she is Muhammad's
2 CONC  biological daughter. Shi'as believe that she is Muhammad's stepdaughter since at the time of her birth Khadija should not have married Prophet Muhammad yet, or that she could not have given birth to all the five children she purp
2 CONC otedly shared with Prophet Muhammad during the time they were married. (Shi'a Ref) She was born three years after the birth of Zainab, when Muhammad was 33.(ref)
