1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Waqid ibn Abdullah ibn Umar ibn al Khattab
2 CONT
2 CONT    His mother was Safiyyah bint Abi 'Ubayd.  He had a son 'Abdullah, whose mother was Amatullah bint 'Abdullah.
2 CONT
2 CONT    Ibn Abi Dhi'b said, "I heard az-Zuhri say that Waqid died in Suqya in ihram and Ibn 'Umar shrouded him in five garments, including a long shirt and turban.:
2 CONT
2 CONT    The father of 'Abdullah ibn Nafi' said, "Waqid ibn 'Abdullah died at Suqya and Ibn Umar prayed over him and buried him.  then he called the bedouins and began to run races between them.  I remarked, 'You buried Waqid a moment a
2 CONC go and now you are racing the bedouins?' He said, 'Woe to you , Nafi', when you see that Allaah has completed a matter, then leave it to Him.'"
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: The Men of Madina Vol. II, Muhammad ibn Sa'd, page 131.
