1 NAME Umm Hakim /Al-Makhzumi/
2 GIVN Umm Hakim
2 SURN Al-Makhzumi
2 _MARNM Al-Makhzumi
1 NAME //
2 GIVN
2 SURN المخزومي
1 SEX F
1 DEAT
2 DATE 634
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From ''Banu Mahkzum'' Tribe.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Umm_Kulthum_bint_Asim
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Umm Hakim (Arabic: أم حكيم‎) (died after 634), was a Sahaba.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was daughter of Harith al Makhzumi (ibn Hisham ibn Mughirah ibn Abdallah ibn Umar ibn Makhzum). She was wife of Ikrimah ibn Abu Jahl,[2][5] he was killed in the Battle of Yarmouk in 634 CE.
2 CONT
2 CONT Later in 634 CE she was married to Abu Said Khalid ibn Said ibn As ibn Umaiyah on the evening preceding battle of Marj al-Saffar, Abu Said was killed in the battle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Later she was married to Umar, from him she had a daughter named Fatimah.
2 CONT
2 CONT Battle of Uhud In the battle of Uhud she accompanied Ikrimah and other Quraish of Mecca who fought against the Muslims. She along with other women, beat drums as they led the group of Quraish women onto the battlefield.[2][5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Conquest of Mecca In 630 CE when the Muslims conquered Mecca, Umm Hakim along with Quraish converted to Islam.[2][5][7] Subsequently Umm Hakim convinced her husband Ikramah to accept Islam.[8]
2 CONT
2 CONT Battle of Marj al-Saffar After Abu Said was killed Umm Hakim single-handedly killed seven Byzantine soldiers with a tent pole near a bridge which is now known as Bridge of Umm Hakim near Damascus,[9] during the battle of Marj al-S
2 CONC affar in 634.
