1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''From Banu 'Adi Clan of Quraysh Tribe.''
2 CONT
2 CONT Source 1: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fatimah_bint_al-Khattab
2 CONT
2 CONT Source 2: Source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banu_Adi
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Fatimah bint al-Khattab was the sister of the second Caliph Umar ibn al-Khattab along with Zayd ibn al-Khattab and one of the early women followers of the Islamic prophet, Muhammad. She was the youngest daughter of Khattab ibn Nuf
2 CONC ayl, who married her off with his nephew, hanif Sa'id ibn Zayd. Fatima along with her husband both converted to Islam together at the same time
2 CONT
2 CONT Sa'īd eventually married Fatimah bint al-Khattab, and both became Muslims and hid their faith from Umar, the wife's brother, until the wife managed to contribute to Umar becoming a Muslim as well.
