1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''From Banu 'Adi Clan of Quraysh Tribe.''
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banu_Adi
2 CONT
2 CONT EVEN BEFORE THE ADVENT OF THE PROPHET GAVE UP IDOLATORY OUT OF OWN CONVICTION;OPENLY ANATHEMATIZED IDOLATORY & HEAPED REPROACHES ON THE CUSTOMS THEN IN VOGUE-INDUCED COUNTRYMEN TO ACCEPT THE FAITH OF ABRAHAM-DUE TO THIS PEOPLE GOT
2 CONC  AGAINST ME AND THE MOST ENERGETIC & UNRELENTING OF ENEMY WAS KHATTAB,THE FATHER OF OMAR,DUE TO HIS SEVERE PERSECUTION,COMPELLED TO FLEE FROM MECCA & TOOK REFUGE IN MOUNTAIN CAVE HIRA.THE FOLLOWING TWO COUPLETS ARE BY ME:
2 CONT
2 CONT 'SHALL I A SINGLE DEITY ADORE 
2 CONT
2 CONT OR SINK IN AWE, ATHOUSAND GODS,BEFORE?
2 CONT
2 CONT THE IDOLS LAT AND UZZA I IGNORE
2 CONT
2 CONT A WISE & CAUTIOUS MAN CAN DO NO MORE.'
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Before Islam, Sa'īd's father, Zayd bin Amr bin Nufayl was a hanif, a follower of the monotheistic tradition of Abraham, and hence never worshipped idols nor ate meat slaughtered in the name of idols. The Quraysh harassed him for t
2 CONC his, and his uncle Khattab bin Nufayl became one of his main tormentors.
2 CONT
2 CONT [Ḥanīf (Arabic: حنيف‎, Ḥanīf; plural: حنفاء, ḥunafā') meaning "revert" refers to one who, according to Islamic belief, maintained the pure monotheism of the patriarch Abraham. More specifically, in Islamic thought, they are the pe
2 CONC ople who, during the period known as the Pre-Islamic period or Age of Ignorance, were seen to have rejected idolatry and retained some or all of the tenets of the religion of Abraham (إبراهيم, Ibrāhīm) which was "submission to God
2 CONC " (Allah) in its purest form]
