1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Zayd ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar ibn al-Khattab
2 CONT
2 CONT    His mother was an umm walad.  His children were Muhammad, Umm Humayd, Umm Zayd, and Fatima, whose mother was Umm Hakim bint Ubaydullah;  'Abdullah, Ibrahim, 'Umar, Fatima and Hafsa whose mother was Hukayma, an umm walad; and Sa
2 CONC wda, whose mother was a Yamani umm walad.  he was the oldest of the children of 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar, and left him while he was still alive.  He went to Kufa and settled there where he died, and he has offspring in Kufa and Yemen. 
2 CONT
2 CONT source: The Men of Madina Vol. II, page 131.
