1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hassan ibn Zeid (829-849) nicknamed The Great Claimer or Daii, is the founder of the Alavid Dynasty in Tabarestan. (voir page 153 de Iranian History at a Glance, Dr. Mahmoud Farrokhpey.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikiwand.com/en/Hasan_ibn_Zayd_ibn_Hasan
2 CONT
2 CONT Al-Ḥasan ibn Zayd ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ‘Alī ibn Abī Ṭālib (died 783), was a notable Alid who served as governor of Medina under al-Mansur.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hasan was the grandson of Hasan, the firstborn son of Ali and Fatimah, the daughter of Muhammad. A pious man, he emulated his father and grandfather in not meddling with the power struggles for the Caliphate, and unlike many Alids
2 CONC  he acquiesced to the Abbasids' seizure of power after the Abbasid Revolution. The first Abbasid Caliph, al-Saffah, married his daughter, and allowed Hasan to live at the court. In 767, al-Saffah's successor al-Mansur appointed Ha
2 CONC san as governor of the holy city of Medina, but dismissed him in 772 after the two fell out, and confiscated his wealth. After al-Mansur died in 775, the new Caliph, al-Mahdi, restored Hasan to his possessions. Hasan died during t
2 CONC he hajj to Mecca in 783, and was buried at al-Hajir.
2 CONT
2 CONT Same profile as : https://www.geni.com/people/Abu-Muhammad-al-Hasan-bin-Zayd-bin-Hasan/6000000000163019773
