1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zayd_ibn_Suhan Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT Zayd ibn Suhan (Arabic: زيد بن صوحان) was a companion of the Islamic prophet Muhammad, and is revered by Shia Muslims. He was the brother of Sa'sa'a bin Sohan. He is mentioned in Sahih al-Bukhari.[1] He was killed in the Battle of
2 CONC  the Camel by Amr Al Yathribi.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Zayd originated from the city of Qatif, Saudi Arabia.
2 CONT
2 CONT His grave and shrine lies in the village of Malkiya in Bahrain. He is sometimes referred to as "Ameer Zayd".
